{{Quote|&hellip;there's something I've always found interesting about this model of interrogation droid. It typically isn't programmed to know anything about a prisoner. All it knows is that you're the one in the cell&mdash;and that means you must be the interview subject. I've had prisoners break when no one's there to listen. They think they're talking to the droid, but it doesn't hear them. You can tell it anything and it doesn't care. It'll just keep working on you until someone tells it to stop.|[[Captain]] [[Khione]]|<ref name="Moving Target: A Princess Leia Adventure">''[[Moving Target: A Princess Leia Adventure]]''</ref>}}
The '''IT-O interrogation droid''', also known as the '''IT-O Interrogation Unit''' or '''IT-O Interrogator''', was an [[Interrogation droid|interrogator droid]] developed by the [[Imperial Department of Military Research]] and utilized by the [[Galactic Empire]].

==History==
{{Quote|Oh hello, IT-O. Big fan of your work.|[[0-0-0]]|<ref name="Aphra 3">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 3|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 3]]</ref>}}
[[File:StarWarsAdventures2020_5_BArt.jpg|left|thumb|279x300px|The IT-O droid was used by the Imperial regime.]]
Developed in secret by the [[Imperial Department of Military Research]],<ref name="DB" /> IT-Os were used by the [[Galactic Empire]] to extract information from prisoners through the use of [[mind probe]]s.<ref name="ANH" /> [[Jedi]], however, were known to have been trained to resist mind probes, requiring the use of other methods to procure information from them.<ref name="Rebel Resolve" /> An IT-O was attempted to be used on [[Avi Singh]] by Captain [[Bragg]], although the Separatist senator was [[Extraction on Raxus|liberated]] before he could be subjected to it.<ref name="Common Ground">{{TBB|Common Ground}}</ref> Another was employed by [[Royce Hemlock]] to torture [[Crosshair|CT-9904]] "Crosshair" in an attempt to locate his former companions [[Clone Force 99]].<ref name="Tipping Point">{{TBB|Tipping Point}}</ref> [[Doctor Ball|One IT-O droid]] was used to interrogate [[Kanan Jarrus]] aboard [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]]'s [[Star Destroyer]] ''[[Sovereign]]''. However, torture was eventually handed over to [[The Grand Inquisitor]].<ref name="Rebel Resolve" /> Another IT-O was used by [[Governor]] [[Arihnda Pryce]] to interrogate the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebel]] [[Hera Syndulla]] after the failed attack on the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Lothal City fuel depot|fuel depot]] for the [[TIE/D Defender Elite]] project.<ref name="Jedi Night">{{Rebels|Jedi Night}}</ref>

An IT-O was later used aboard the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] to extract information from [[Prince]]ss [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], although she proved to have considerable resistance to the mind probe.<ref name="ANH" /> The IT-O was later deployed on [[Yavin 4]] during the Empire's cleanup operations at the former [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Alliance]] [[Great Temple|base]].<ref name="Aphra 3" />

By [[9 ABY]], at least one as lab droid reprogrammed white-painted IT-O was active on the planet of [[Plazir-15]]. The IT-O unit worked alongside a [[Unidentified lab tech (Plazir-15)|lab tech]] in a morgue, where they received a [[Unidentified rogue B2-series battle droid|rogue]] [[B2-series super battle droid]]. The IT-O unit however, attacked its master when it was infected with [[NM-K reconstitutor|nanodroids]] planted by [[Commissioner]] [[Helgait]]. The droid was destroyed by [[Din Djarin]] with the [[Darksaber]] before it could deal any major damage.<ref name="Chapter 22">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 22: Guns for Hire}}</ref>

Decades later, the [[First Order]] used a [[IT-000 interrogator droid|new model]] of interrogator droid that harked back to the IT-O model.<ref name="IT-000 DB">{{Databank|first-order-interrogator-droid|First Order Interrogator Droid}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
[[File:IT-O_Interrogation_Unit.jpg|thumb|right|300px|IT-O units were commonly used by the Galactic Empire.]]
The IT-0 was designed around a small spherical repulsor-equipped casing. Around this casing there were a multitude of devices, based on standard [[medical droid]] equipment, but modified to cause pain and biological degradation to subjects instead of curing them. These devices included a [[sonic torture device]], an [[electroshock nerve probe]] on top of the droid's frame as well as a drug injector syringe, prominently mounted on the droid's side and designed to be as large -and therefore intimidating- as possible. Other equipment included a chemical torture turret, deployable [[flesh peeler]]s and [[joint crippler]]s, a [[mind probe]], and a [[truth serum]].<ref name="TCVDNE">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref>

The droid was [[Sentience|non-sentient]] and designed only to continuously inflict [[torture]] upon its subjects until instructed to stop doing so. Although it was equipped with a red [[Victim analysis photoreceptor/Canon|victim analysis photoreceptor]] and assorted [[biofeedback monitor]]s which allowed it to accurately determine whether the victim was telling the truth or not, it could not actually act on this information and would merely relay it to a superior officer.<ref name="Moving Target">''[[Moving Target: A Princess Leia Adventure]]''</ref>

